# Project Assignment pages

Student-facing Project specs. Copy from `templates/Project Assignment.md` into `Module NN - Topic/Project NN - Title.md`. Match Project 01 (Quiz Game) and Project 02 (Course Registration Simulator).

## Placement

| Project | Module folder |
|---------|----------------|
| 01 | Module 03 - Conditionals and Functions |
| 02 | Module 06 - Data Structures |
| 03 | Module 09 - Classes |
| 04 | Module 12 - Fancy Data Structures |

## Fill rules

| Placeholder | Value |
|-------------|--------|
| `{{NN}}` / `{{Title}}` | Two-digit id and short title |
| `{{OVERVIEW_PARAGRAPH}}` | What to build + which skills it shows |
| `{{COMPLETE_LIST}}` | What students submit (one option, or all core requirements) |
| `{{WALKTHROUGH_VIDEO}}` | Embed/link, or `*[Insert walkthrough video about completing programming projects]*` |
| `{{ACCEPT_LINK}}` | Always `[INSERT ASSIGNMENT LINK]` on the student page |
| `{{REQUIREMENTS_LIST}}` | Core / option bullets (shared bullets stay in the template) |
| `{{GRADING_NOTE}}` | Extra 90% note if needed (extensions, `Additional requirements:`) |
| `{{PROGRAMMING_PROBLEMS}}` | Options or a single required program |
| `{{CHECKLIST_ITEMS}}` | One checklist line per required completion (`- ☐ …`) |

Do **not** put a starter-template line or a live accept URL on the student Project page. Instructors paste the link in the LMS / when publishing.

## GitHub block (not Classroom)

Say **GitHub**, not Classroom or classroom50, on student pages:

```markdown
## 🚀 GitHub

Open the GitHub assignment using the link below.

**GitHub Assignment**

[INSERT ASSIGNMENT LINK]
```

Always keep the WARNING: submit the **repository** URL, not Codespaces / `github.dev`.

## Checklists

Markdown task lists (`- [ ]`) do **not** copy cleanly into Blackboard. Always use the ballot-box emoji:

```markdown
- ☐ Menu loop works until exit
- ☐ Correct file name (`project02.py`)
```

Never use `- [ ]` or `- [x]` in Project pages.

## Grading and file name

- Include the 90% vs above-90% table (core = up to 90%; meaningful extension = above 90%).
- One file: `project{{NN}}.py`, except **Project 04** grades `main.py` in the chatbot starter.
- Reuse the template AI Disclosure block. Do not invent a second set.
- Project 04: tell students to set Python **3.12.1**; do not put the live accept URL or env3d starter URL on the student page.

## Voice and LMS

- Student voice; Blackboard = LMS URL submission.
- No em dashes.

## Sync

After adding a Project, wire it into that module’s Overview, README, and the Course Map Project row.
